<task id="055" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>The collision prompt must name the document it would write into, and must not silently discard the selected record</title>
    <phase>2 Save flow</phase>
    <gate>startable — deps 025 ✅, 026 ✅, 054 ✅ are all merged</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies `.cs` and `.tsx` on the deployed Office save spine; tags include bff-api + security. Widens an error body, which is an authorization-disclosure question, not a cosmetic change.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive judgment (escalation trigger (b) asks whether a name/association in a 409 body is a disclosure the caller cannot already obtain), plus half (2) is a contract DESIGN decision with two legitimate shapes — not a mechanical edit against a canonical reference.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>`OfficeService.cs` is shared with tasks 014/025/031/052 and `SaveFlow.tsx` with 025/045/053; `unified-access-control-r2` is also live on the Office surface per projects/INDEX.md. Run /conflict-check before opening the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>025, 026, 054</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, frontend, fluent-ui, office-addins, save-flow, spe, data-integrity, security, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Fix GitHub #1005 / ISS-006: the pane's "Save as new version" collision retry writes into whichever document happens to own the colliding FILE NAME, without naming it, and silently discards the user's selected Related-to record. Make the refusal name its target, and stop discarding an explicit user selection. Both halves land together or neither does.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expertise in the BFF Office save spine (`OfficeService.SaveAsync` and its refusal paths), RFC-7807 ProblemDetails contracts, Dataverse lookup resolution, and Fluent UI v9 task-pane surfaces. Follow ADRs strictly, and treat the authorization question in the escalation section as a first-class part of the work rather than a footnote.</role>

  <goal>A filename collision refusal tells the user WHICH document it would write into — by name and by what that document is filed to — and the pane never silently throws away a Related-to record the user explicitly selected. The existing non-destructive guarantee of task 025 is unchanged: a refusal still writes nothing.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Diagnosed live 2026-09-18 during task 042 UAT. Full evidence chain:
      `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/042-uat-findings-2026-09-18.md`. Filed as
      [#1005](https://github.com/spaarke-dev/spaarke/issues/1005) / ISS-006 in `notes/defer-issues.md`.

      A create save whose file name collides is refused with `OFFICE_020` — and that refusal is CORRECT:
      `ConflictBehavior.Fail` means SPE refuses the PUT atomically and no bytes move. Task 025 built this and
      it works.

      The defect is what the pane offers NEXT. The 409 carries `existingDocumentId`, resolved purely by
      matching `sprk_graphdriveid` + `sprk_filename`. The pane shows "Save as new version" whenever that id is
      present and versions the open document onto it. Because `WordAdapter.getSubject()` falls back to
      `'Untitled Document'` (Word's Title metadata property, which is normally blank) and containers are
      BUSINESS-UNIT scoped with a flat root, `Untitled Document.docx` is a single shared name slot for an
      entire business unit — so the resolved "existing document" is routinely an unrelated document belonging
      to someone else. Observed live: a patent document was written as a new SPE version of an unrelated
      orphan row, profiled, and RAG-indexed under that row, while the matter the user had selected in the pane
      received nothing at all.

      THE BUG IS NOT THE DROPPED ASSOCIATION. `useSaveFlow.ts:937-941`
      (`const sentEntity = versionTarget ? null : selectedEntity`) omits `targetEntity` on a version save
      DELIBERATELY and CORRECTLY per task 023 D-4/D-5 — a version save writes to the existing document's own
      item and re-associating it would both be inert and add an authorization check that could refuse a
      legitimate version save. THE BUG IS THAT A FILENAME MATCH IS BEING TREATED AS DOCUMENT IDENTITY, and
      that the pane then discards an explicit user selection without saying so.

      TWO HALVES — BOTH REQUIRED, THEY MUST LAND TOGETHER (half 1 alone still discards the selection; half 2
      alone still leaves the target unnamed):
      (1) NAME THE TARGET. The refusal must carry enough for the pane to state WHICH document it would write
          into — the document's name and what it is filed to — so the user can see it is not theirs. Today
          only an opaque GUID crosses the wire.
      (2) STOP SILENTLY DISCARDING THE USER'S CHOICE. Either do not offer the version retry when the colliding
          document's association contradicts the user's selected Related-to record, or carry `targetEntity`
          through and refuse server-side with a typed error. Silently dropping an explicit selection is not
          acceptable under either shape. Choose ONE, and record why in the note.
    </background>
