  <justification>
    <existing>`SaveError` (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/Office/SaveResponse.cs:104`) already carries the collision's `FileName` (:130) and `ExistingDocumentId` (:140), and `MapSaveErrorToProblem`'s `NameCollision` arm (`OfficeEndpoints.cs:558-570`) already emits both as ProblemDetails extensions. On the client, `describeCollisionFailure` (`errorMessages.ts:362-374`) already threads them into `ErrorMessage`. For the display data, `DocumentUrlIdentityResolution.ResolveRelatedRecordDisplayAsync` (task 026) already resolves displayName/number for the same four direct slots with a settled precedence and handles the primary-name trap.</existing>
    <extension>YES — extend all of the above. The new fields are ADDITIVE properties on the existing `SaveError` record and the existing extensions dictionary, mirroring exactly how task 025 added `FileName`/`ExistingDocumentId`. No new endpoint, no new error code, no new resolver, no second lookup: widen the ONE existing `FindDocumentIdByLocationAsync` projection rather than issuing a second query.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A user clicking the button the pane offers writes their document into an unrelated document's SPE item and Dataverse row, which is then profiled and RAG-indexed under that row — making content readable and AI-queryable by people who were never granted it — while the record they selected receives nothing and they are shown "saved". This is observed behaviour on the deployed dev build (2026-09-18), not a hypothetical.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the two halves in `&lt;background&gt;` MUST land together. Shipping half (1) alone still discards the user's selection; shipping half (2) alone still leaves the target unnamed. A PR containing only one is not this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — task 025's non-destructive invariant is unchanged and MUST stay true: a refused collision writes no bytes, creates no `sprk_document` row, and leaves the existing item's bytes and version count untouched. This task changes only what the refusal SAYS and what the pane OFFERS.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — half (1) resolves display data by widening the EXISTING `OfficeDocumentPersistence.FindDocumentIdByLocationAsync` projection (it matches `sprk_graphdriveid` + `sprk_filename`, constants at `OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs:33-34`) and/or by reusing task 026's `ResolveRelatedRecordDisplayAsync`. MUST NOT add a second Dataverse lookup, a second display resolver, or a second collision detector (root CLAUDE.md §11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — files this task MUST NOT change: `Services/Office/ContentDedupDetector.cs`, `Api/OBOEndpoints.cs`, `src/client/shared/Spaarke.SdapClient/**`, `src/solutions/DocumentUploadWizard/**`. Verify with `git diff --name-only` and state it in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — `OfficeImmutableSaveFileSafetyTests` and `OfficeEmailSaveNamingTests` MUST pass UNMODIFIED. They encode a live-on-master data-loss fix; task 054 was held to the same bar. Editing them to make this task pass is a failure, not a fix.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the version-save WRITE semantics of task 023 (an item-keyed OBO write to the resolved row, which never re-associates) are NOT this task's to change. See escalation trigger (a).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">SCOPE — the collision refusal stays a typed ProblemDetails the client branches on. New fields are additive extensions on the EXISTING `OfficeErrorCodes.NameCollision` arm of `MapSaveErrorToProblem`; do not introduce a new error code and do not change `OFFICE_020`'s status, type URI, or `retryable` value.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">SCOPE — any authorization decision about what the widened 409 body may reveal is made on the endpoint's existing filter chain, not invented inside the service. Note that `ExistingDocumentId` is ALREADY returned today, so the question is specifically whether NAME and ASSOCIATION are a further disclosure. See escalation trigger (b).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE — all collision UI in the pane: Fluent UI v9 semantic tokens only, no hex literals, legible in both Office themes via `useOfficeTheme`. The refusal keeps `intent="warning"`, never `"error"` — a collision is a choice, not a failure (task 025's copy convention, pinned by `errorMessages.collision.test.ts`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">SCOPE — this add-in package only, per the project's standing Path A exception: MUST NOT import `@spaarke/ui-components`. This explicitly rules out `ChoiceDialog` and `.claude/patterns/ui/choice-dialog-pattern.md` as the reference — see `&lt;knowledge&gt;` for the correct in-repo anchor.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">SCOPE — any Dataverse GUID crossing a boundary in this task is canonicalized bare-lowercase via the shared `cleanGuid` before it leaves the client, and is never interpolated raw into an OData key predicate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">SCOPE — the widened `OFFICE_020` response shape gets contract coverage in the existing Office contract suite. Cite `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md` — there is no concise copy in `.claude/adr/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — NFR-03: `Xrm.*` does not exist in an Office host; MUST NOT import any Xrm-bound component. NFR-10: any host difference is expressed as an adapter CAPABILITY, never a `hostType` conditional inside a view.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — BFF publish size: measure the delta against a FRESH BUILD of `origin/master`, never the recorded baseline number (root CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4). Zip both with PowerShell `Compress-Archive -Optimal` (matching `scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1`) and report both absolute sizes, the delta, and the tool name.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — build commands for `src/client/office-addins` only: install with `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`; there is NO `build:prod` script in this package — `npm run build` IS the production build.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the PR description MUST state the Placement Justification for the BFF-side change per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`, cite #1005, and record which shape of half (2) was chosen and why.</constraint>
  </constraints>

