  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/CLAUDE.md`, the findings note, and the knowledge files above. Output the mandatory rigor declaration (FULL, opus, xhigh, directional) per root CLAUDE.md §8. Run `/conflict-check` — `OfficeService.cs` and `SaveFlow.tsx` are contended surfaces.</step>
    <step order="1">Read the findings note §3 and confirm the six-step mechanism against the CODE yourself before changing anything. If your reading contradicts the note, say so and stop — an empirical disagreement about the save path is a §F.3 reproduce-first situation, not something to paper over.</step>
    <step order="2">ANSWER ESCALATION TRIGGER (b) EXPLICITLY AND IN WRITING BEFORE WRITING THE SERVER CHANGE. The 409 already returns the colliding document's GUID today. Determine, from the endpoint's filter chain and the existing authorization model, whether adding its NAME and its ASSOCIATION is a further disclosure to a caller who may hold no rights on that document. Record the answer in the note with the evidence. If it IS a further disclosure, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than shipping it.</step>
    <step order="3">Reproduce-first (§F.3): add the failing tests BEFORE the fix — a client test proving the pane offers to version a document it never names, and a server contract test proving the 409 carries no name/association. Show them failing for the RIGHT reason and record the failure text.</step>
    <step order="4">Half (1) server: widen the existing `FindDocumentIdByLocationAsync` projection (or reuse task 026's `ResolveRelatedRecordDisplayAsync`) so `ResolveNameCollisionAsync` can populate new ADDITIVE display fields on `SaveError` (`SaveResponse.cs:104`), and emit them from the existing `OfficeErrorCodes.NameCollision` arm of `MapSaveErrorToProblem` (`OfficeEndpoints.cs:558-570`). Do not add a second lookup or a second resolver.</step>
    <step order="5">Half (1) client: thread the new fields through `describeCollisionFailure` (`errorMessages.ts:362-374`) into `ErrorMessage`, and render them in `renderCollisionState` so the button reads as an action against a NAMED document ("Save as a new version of {name} — filed to {record}"). Preserve the existing behaviour when the server resolved nothing: only "Keep both" is offered.</step>
    <step order="6">Half (2): implement the chosen shape — either withhold the version retry when the colliding document's association contradicts the user's selected Related-to record, or carry `targetEntity` and refuse server-side with a typed error. Whichever is chosen, an explicit user selection is never silently discarded. Record the decision and the rejected alternative in the note.</step>
    <step order="7">Extend the EXISTING test files — `SaveFlowCollision.test.tsx` (6 tests today, including "a collision with no resolvable existing document offers ONLY Keep both" at :194-207) and `errorMessages.collision.test.ts` (6 pure-function tests) — plus the Office contract suite. Do not fork a parallel test file.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `npm run typecheck` (expect the 111 total / 0 production baseline), the gated jest suites, `npm run build`; and `dotnet build` plus the full `Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests`, ArchTests, and the Office contract + integration suites. Confirm `OfficeImmutableSaveFileSafetyTests` and `OfficeEmailSaveNamingTests` are green AND unmodified (`git diff --name-only`).</step>
    <step order="9">Measure BFF publish size against a fresh `origin/master` build per the constraint; record both absolute sizes, the delta, and the zip tool in `notes/055-publish-size.md`.</step>
    <step order="10">Run code-review + adr-check per task-execute Step 9.5.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (status → ✅) and write `notes/055-collision-names-its-target.md` recording: the trigger-(b) authorization answer, which shape of half (2) was chosen and the alternative rejected, and the reproduce-first failure text.</step>
    <step order="12">Update `notes/defer-issues.md` ISS-006 and comment on #1005 with the outcome. Do not close the issue until the fix is verified on a deployed build — this project's own ISS-005 precedent kept the issue open until live confirmation.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>(a) If the fix would require making a VERSION save re-associate the document to the caller's selected record — STOP and escalate. That silently re-files another user's document onto the current user's record, which is worse than the defect being fixed, and it crosses the ADR-008 authorization boundary task 023 D-4/D-5 deliberately avoided. Half (2) must be solved by withholding the offer or by refusing, never by re-associating.</trigger>
    <trigger>(b) If returning the colliding document's NAME or ASSOCIATION in the 409 body would disclose something the caller cannot already read — STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6. Task 025's own POML flagged "the 409 body would need to reveal the existing document's id or owner" as an enumeration concern, and this task widens exactly that body. Note the id is ALREADY returned today, so the question is narrowly whether name and association are a FURTHER disclosure. This must be answered in writing at step 2, before any server code is written.</trigger>
    <trigger>(c) If `/conflict-check` shows `OfficeService.cs`, `OfficeEndpoints.cs` or `SaveFlow.tsx` being modified concurrently by another worktree (`unified-access-control-r2` is live on the Office surface), STOP, rebase, and re-run before opening the PR.</trigger>
    <trigger>(d) If making the refusal name its target would require a second Dataverse round-trip on the refusal path that measurably changes the refusal's latency profile, STOP and surface the trade-off rather than silently accepting it — the refusal is on the user's interactive save path.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="The prompt names a document that is NOT the user's, and declining is easy">
      <steps>
        <step>Arrange a document in the business-unit container named `Untitled Document.docx` that is filed to a DIFFERENT record than the one under test (or to no record at all).</step>
        <step>In Word, open a new document with no Title property set, select a Related-to record in the pane, and save.</step>
        <step>Read the collision message and both action buttons.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The refusal names the colliding document — its name and what it is filed to — so the user can tell it is not theirs. Either the "Save as new version" action is not offered (because its association contradicts the selection), or choosing it does not silently discard the selected record. Dismissing writes nothing: no bytes, no `sprk_document` row, no SPE version.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="The prompt when the colliding document legitimately IS the user's own">
      <steps>
        <step>Save a document to a record, then save a second document with the SAME name to the SAME record.</step>
        <step>Read the collision message, then choose "Save as new version".</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The named document is recognisably the user's own and filed to the record they selected, so the offer reads as correct. Choosing it writes a new SPE version of that document and creates no second row — task 023's version path, unchanged by this task.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark-mode check via the Office theme toggle">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the Office theme to Dark, reload the pane, trigger the collision, and view the message including the newly added document-name line.</step>
        <step>Repeat in Light mode. Also view it with a very long document name.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Every colour resolves from a Fluent v9 semantic token with legible contrast in both themes; no hex literals in the added styles; the message keeps `intent="warning"`, never `"error"`; and a long document name wraps or ellipsises without breaking the narrow pane layout or hiding the action buttons.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

