  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the colliding name is owned by a resolvable `sprk_document`, when the save is refused, then the 409 ProblemDetails carries that document's NAME and its ASSOCIATION (what it is filed to) in addition to the `fileName` and `existingDocumentId` it already carries — asserted by a contract test on the response body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given that 409 reaches the pane, when the collision message renders, then it names the document it would write into and what that document is filed to — asserted by a render test, not by reading the message string out of `detail`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a colliding document whose association CONTRADICTS the user's selected Related-to record, when the collision message renders, then the user's explicit selection is not silently discarded: either the version retry is not offered, or it is offered and the selection is honoured/refused explicitly. Assert whichever shape was implemented, and assert the negative — that a silent drop does not occur.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the server could NOT resolve an owning document (an unreferenced SPE item), when the collision message renders, then ONLY "Keep both" is offered and no name is claimed — the existing behaviour pinned by `SaveFlowCollision.test.tsx:194-207` and `errorMessages.collision.test.ts` ("omits collisionExistingDocumentId…") is UNCHANGED.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (non-destructive invariant, task 025): given any refused collision, when the flow completes, then the existing item's bytes and version count are unchanged, no `sprk_document` row is created or updated, and no SPE item is deleted — asserted by reading them before and after.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (authorization): the trigger-(b) question is answered in writing in `notes/055-collision-names-its-target.md` with evidence from the endpoint's filter chain BEFORE the server change, and a test asserts that a caller who cannot read the colliding document does not receive its name or association.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (no re-association): `git diff` shows the version-save write path still sends no `targetEntity`, and no code path re-associates an existing document to the caller's selected record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`OFFICE_020` keeps its status code, type URI and `retryable: false`; no new error code is introduced; the refusal still renders `intent="warning"`, never `"error"`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reproduce-first: the new tests are shown FAILING for the right reason before the fix, and the failure text is recorded in the note; all of them pass after.</criterion>
